The improvement is **Redis Consumer Groups**.

Right now your tracking service reads the stream like this:

```python
xread(...)
```

This works, but it has a **serious architectural limitation**.

If your tracking service crashes or you scale multiple workers, you may:

```text
lose messages
process messages twice
create race conditions
```

Production systems solve this using **consumer groups**.

---

# 1. Concept: Consumer Groups

Redis streams support **Kafka-like consumer groups**.

Instead of:

```text
producer → stream → single consumer
```

we get:

```text
producer → stream → consumer group → multiple workers
```

Example:

```text
vision_service → vision_detections
                        │
                        ▼
                 tracking_group
                    │     │
               worker1  worker2
```

Redis ensures each message is delivered to **one worker only**.

---

# 2. Why This Matters Architecturally

Consumer groups enable:

```text
horizontal scaling
fault tolerance
message acknowledgement
```

These are core concepts in:

* Kafka
* Flink
* Spark Streaming
* real-time ML systems

You are essentially building a **mini streaming platform**.

